Let me try with a general lambda to see if we can fix it\nlam = sp.Symbol('lam', negative=True)\n\n# Actually, let me try a different approach.\n# The issue might be fixable by choosing a different lambda.\n# Or better: try a COUPLED form ψ = a*t - b*(x+x0)^2 (quadratic in x, linear in t)\n# This is one of the suggested ansatz families and hasn't been tried yet.\n\n# Quadratic ansatz: ψ = a*t - (x + x0)^2\n# psi_t = a, psi_x = -2(x+x0), psi_tt = 0, psi_xx = -2\n# box_psi = 0 - c^2*(-2) = 2c^2\n# tilde_box_psi = a^2 - c^2*4*(x+x0)^2\n\n# With alpha=1:\n# L/phi = lam^2*(a^2 - 4c^2*(x+x0)^2)\n# L1/phi = lam^2*(a^2 + 4c^2*(x+x0)^2) + lam*(0 + c^2*(-2)) = lam^2*(a^2+4c^2*(x+x0)^2) - 2c^2*lam\n\n# (L-L1)/phi = -8*c^2*lam^2*(x+x0)^2 + 2c^2*lam\n# For this to be >= 0: 2c^2*lam >= 8c^2*lam^2*(x+x0)^2\n# => lam >= 4*lam^2*(x+x0)^2 (since lam < 0, dividing flips inequality)\n# Actually lam < 0, so 2c^2*lam < 0 and -8c^2*lam^2*(x+x0)^2 < 0\n# Sum of two negatives => (L-L1)/phi < 0 always! FAILS.\n\n# So quadratic in x with alpha=1 fails condition 1a.\n# Try alpha != 1 with quadratic.\n\n# ψ = a*t - (x+x0)^2, general alpha\n# L/phi = lam^2*(a^2 - 4c^2*(x+x0)^2) - (alpha-1)*lam*2c^2\n# L1/phi = lam^2*(a^2 + 4c^2*(x+x0)^2) + lam*(-2c^2)\n\n# (L-L1)/phi = -8c^2*lam^2*(x+x0)^2 - (alpha-1)*lam*2c^2 + 2c^2*lam\n# = -8c^2*lam^2*(x+x0)^2 + 2c^2*lam*(1-(alpha-1))\n# = -8c^2*lam^2*(x+x0)^2 + 2c^2*lam*(2-alpha)\n\n# For this ≥ 0: 2c^2*lam*(2-alpha) >= 8c^2*lam^2*(x+x0)^2\n# With lam < 0: lam*(2-alpha) must be positive, so (2-alpha) < 0, i.e. alpha > 2\n# Then: |lam|*(alpha-2) >= 4*lam^2*(x+x0)^2 => (alpha-2)/|lam| >= 4*(x+x0)^2\n# But (x+x0)^2 grows without bound as x->inf. FAILS for any finite alpha, lam.\n\nprint(\"Quadratic in x fails condition 1a for any alpha (unbounded x).\")\nprint()\n\n# Go back to separated log form but try to fix L2.\n# Key insight: the L2 issue comes from the fact that with alpha=1,\n# box_psi = psi_tt - c^2*psi_xx = 1/(1+t)^2 - c^2/(1+x)^2\n# and tilde_box_psi = psi_t^2 - c^2*psi_x^2 = same thing!\n# So box_psi = tilde_box_psi for our log-log ansatz.\n\n# What if we use alpha != 1 to tune L2?\n# With alpha != 1:\n# L/phi = lam^2*tilde_box_psi - (alpha-1)*lam*box_psi\n# Since tilde_box_psi = box_psi for our ansatz:\n# L/phi = (lam^2 - (alpha-1)*lam) * box_psi = lam*(lam - alpha + 1)*box_psi\n\n# L1/phi = lam^2*(psi_t^2 + c^2*psi_x^2) + lam*(psi_tt + c^2*psi_xx)\n# = lam^2*(1/(1+t)^2 + c^2/(1+x)^2) + lam*(-1/(1+t)^2 - c^2/(1+x)^2)\n# = (lam^2 - lam)*(1/(1+t)^2 + c^2/(1+x)^2)\n# = lam*(lam-1)*(1/(1+t)^2 + c^2/(1+x)^2)\n\n# With lam < 0: lam*(lam-1) = lam^2 - lam > 0, so L1/phi > 0\n# For condition 1: L1 <= 0, we need L1/phi <= 0\n# But lam*(lam-1) > 0 for lam < 0 (since lam < 0, lam-1 < 0, product positive)\n# So L1/phi > 0, meaning L1 > 0, which VIOLATES condition 1!\n\n# Wait, condition 1 says L1 <= L <= -L1, which implies L1 <= 0.\n# We need L1/phi <= 0. \n# L1/phi = (lam^2 + lam)*gradient_term + lam*(psi_tt + c^2*psi_xx)... \n# Actually I had the wrong sign. Let me redo:\n# L1/phi = lam^2*(psi_t^2 + c^2*psi_x^2) + lam*(psi_tt + c^2*psi_xx)\n# psi_t = -1/(1+t), psi_x = -1/(1+x)\n# psi_t^2 + c^2*psi_x^2 = 1/(1+t)^2 + c^2/(1+x)^2 > 0\n# psi_tt + c^2*psi_xx = 1/(1+t)^2 + c^2/(1+x)^2 > 0 ... wait\n# psi_tt = d/dt(-1/(1+t)) = 1/(1+t)^2\n# psi_xx = d/dx(-1/(1+x)) = 1/(1+x)^2\n# psi_tt + c^2*psi_xx = 1/(1+t)^2 + c^2/(1+x)^2 > 0\n\n# So L1/phi = lam^2*P + lam*Q where P = Q = 1/(1+t)^2 + c^2/(1+x)^2 > 0\n# = (lam^2 + lam)*P = lam*(lam+1)*P\n\n# For L1 <= 0: lam*(lam+1) <= 0\n# lam < 0, so need lam+1 >= 0, i.e. lam >= -1\n# So -1 <= lam < 0.\n# With lam = -1/10: lam*(lam+1) = (-1/10)(9/10) = -9/100 < 0. OK!\n\n# Actually wait, I had the right formula before. Let me recheck Round 1.\n# In round 1, L1/phi was computed as:\n# lam^2*((psi_t)^2 + c^2*(psi_x)^2) + lam*(psi_tt + c^2*psi_xx)\n# For the log-log: = (1/100)(P) + (-1/10)(P) = (1/100 - 1/10)*P = -9/100 * P < 0 ✓\n# Good, L1 <= 0 is satisfied.\n\nprint(\"For log-log with lam=-1/10:\")\nprint(\"L1/phi = (-9/100) * (1/(1+t)^2 + c^2/(1+x)^2) < 0 ✓\")\nprint()\n\n# Now the question: can we adjust lambda to fix L2?\n# Let me try smaller |lambda| values, like -1/100\nprint(\"Testing log-log with different lambda values for L2...\")\nPYEOF\n","description":"Analyze L2 failure structure and alternatives","timeout":60000}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2008,"cache_read_input_tokens":112543,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2008,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0a4aefa-94cf-4571-b6fe-4e02cd213274","uuid":"ce4715ac-9ffe-41ae-ae65-c6916e48145d"}
